      "source": "https://crownpointlibrary.org/research/indianaroom/if-solon-could-see-us-now/its-indianas-bicentennial-200-fun-facts-about-crown-point-to-celebrate/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1934, John Dillinger escaped from the Lake County Jail in Crown Point, a daring break that drew national attention.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crown_Point%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 2008 Universal Studios shoot filmed “Public Enemies” at the former jail, bringing Hollywood to Crown Point’s historic site.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crown_Point%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Every summer, Crown Point hosts the Corn Roast and Taste of Crown Point festivals, celebrating local food and music around the historic courthouse.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crown_Point%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Wellington Clark House, Crown Point’s oldest intact home, stands as a living testament to the town’s early architectural heritage.",
